      </Card>

      {/* Why Web Workers? */}
      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
            <div className="p-2 rounded-lg bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-900/30">
              <Clock className="w-5 h-5 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <CardTitle>The Problem: JavaScript is Single-Threaded</CardTitle>
              <CardDescription>Why your UI freezes during heavy operations</CardDescription>
            </div>
          </div>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="space-y-4">
          <p className="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            JavaScript runs on a <strong>single thread</strong>. When you execute a heavy computation (like processing large data, image manipulation, or complex calculations), the entire browser freezes - buttons don't work, animations stop, and users can't interact with your app.
          </p>
          
          <div className="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
